Modified files
--------------

body_middle_top_usbc.stl (and body_middle_top_usbc.step, generated)
  Derived from print/body_middle_top.stl of the repository above.
  CHANGED by heypcb-kicad's boards/quack_core/cad/fit.py, 2026-10-02: one
  13.0 x 7.5 mm opening with 1.5 mm corner radii was cut through the right-hand
  (-y) side wall, centred on the Quack Core board's USB-C receptacle at CAD
  x -62.0, z -2.87 (research spec item B2). Nothing else was changed. The STEP
  is a faceted solid sewn from the STL's triangles.
  fit.py writes both files to build/quack_core/cad/ each time it runs. The STL
  in this directory is the one it wrote on 2026-10-02. The STEP (about 12 MB,
  one face per triangle) is not committed; run fit.py to regenerate it.

Unmodified inputs
-----------------

fit.py reads the print STLs and URDF meshes of the repository above from a
local copy (robots/research/duck/cad/). It does not redistribute them.

